## Why This Is Asked
Tests a concrete DP state definition on strings with reconstruction and space-time trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- DP state: dp[i][t] for substring ending at i with t flips
- Transitions handle 1 vs 0 at i; reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space: O(nk) both; can optimize space

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxOnesWithFlips(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const start = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      if (s[i] === '1') {
        dp[i][t] = (i > 0 ? dp[i-1][t] : 0) + 1;
        start[i][t] = (i > 0 ? start[i-1][t] : i);
      } else if (t > 0) {
        dp[i][t] = (i > 0 ? dp[i-1][t-0 - 1] : 0) + 1;
        start[i][t] = (i > 0 ? start[i-1][t-1] : i);
      } else {
        dp[i][t] = 0;
        start[i][t] = -1;
      }
    }
  }
  // find max and reconstruct
  return {len: 0, l:0, r:0};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you reconstruct the exact substring without extra storage?
- How would you optimize space further?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests DP over partitioning with an order-dependent gain, plus reconstruction. Distinct from standard sum-of-maximums or cooldown problems.

## Key Concepts

- Order-dependent block weighting
- Prefix sums for O(1) subarray sums
- 2D DP with backtracking pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and reconstruction

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxValue(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      // end a block at i
      for (let j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
        const val = dp[j][t-1] + (pref[i+1] - pref[j]) * t;
        if (val > dp[i+1][t]) {
          dp[i+1][t] = val;
          par[i+1][t] = j;
        }
      }
      // skip i is implicit via dp[i+1][t] initialization from dp[i][t]
      if (dp[i][t] > dp[i+1][t]) {
        dp[i+1][t] = dp[i][t];
        par[i+1][t] = -2; // indicate skip
      }
    }
  }
  // Reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return dp[n][k];
}
```

